## 🧠 Reflection

Day 15 made me realize that write-intensive skills like Apex and LWC are only as valuable as the underlying data they interact with. Building an incredibly fast web component means nothing if the fields it displays are corrupted, duplicated, or missing entirely. 

Learning the exact order of operations required for enterprise migrations highlighted the value of structured thinking. It forced me to map out complex lookup paths before writing import scripts. Moving forward, prioritizing declarative tools like Duplicate Rules and backing them up with native database field uniqueness constraints will ensure the custom architectures we build remain clean, reliable, and highly functional for enterprise business users.
